---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import BrowserVersionChecker from '@/components/tools/reference/BrowserVersionChecker.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="browser-version-checker">
  <BrowserVersionChecker client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the browser version checker works</h2>
    <p>
      The browser version checker reads the user agent string that your browser gives every page, and
      the User-Agent Client Hints where the browser supports them. It finds the browser, its version and
      the operating system, and compares the version with the latest stable release. Both values come
      from your browser; the page does not send them anywhere.
    </p>
    <p>
      The latest versions come from the release feeds of Chrome, Firefox and Edge and from the browser
      data of MDN, which also covers Safari, Opera and Samsung Internet. The site refreshes them each
      week, so a release from the last few days can be missing.
    </p>
    <h2>Why an up-to-date browser matters</h2>
    <p>
      Each browser release fixes security holes that are often public by the time the update ships.
      Chrome, Edge and Firefox release a new major version about every four weeks, and roll it out to
      users over a week or two. Safari updates come with macOS, iOS and iPadOS updates.
    </p>
    <h2>Browsers on iPhone and iPad</h2>
    <p>
      On iOS and iPadOS, browsers use the WebKit engine of the system. Chrome or Firefox on an iPhone is
      as current as the Safari version of that iOS release, so the checker compares the Safari version.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
